## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of identity-based security, secret management, and infrastructure as code in a beginner Azure context, with emphasis on environment isolation, governance, and CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Managed identities and Key Vault access policies
- Environment isolation with separate Key Vaults
- Tagging governance and policy enforcement
- Bicep/ARM IaC deployment and GitHub Actions

## Code Example

```bicep
// Minimal example showing a Function App identity and Key Vault access
resource kv 'Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults@2021-04-01-preview' = {
  name: 'kv-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  properties: {
    tenantId: subscription().tenantId
    sku: {
      family: 'A'
      name: 'standard'
    }
    accessPolicies: [
      {
        tenantId: subscription().tenantId
        objectId: functionIdentity.properties.principalId
        permissions: {
          secrets: [
            'get'
            'list'
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
    tags: {
      Environment: environment
      Project: projectName
      Owner: ownerTag
    }
  }
}

resource functionIdentity 'Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities@2023-01-31' = {
  name: 'func-identity-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  tags: {
    Environment: environment
    Project: projectName
  }
}

resource functionApp 'Microsoft.Web/sites@2022-03-01' = {
  name: 'func-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  kind: 'functionapp'
  identity: {
    type: 'UserAssigned'
    userAssignedIdentities: {
      '${functionIdentity.id}': {}
    }
  }
  properties: {
    serverFarmId: appServicePlan.id
    siteConfig: {
      appSettings: [
        {
          name: 'KEY_VAULT_NAME'
          value: kv.name
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  tags: {
    Environment: environment
    Project: projectName
  }
}
```

## GitHub Actions Workflow

```yaml
name: Deploy Azure Resources

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:

env:
  ENVIRONMENT: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && 'prod' || 'dev' }}

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      id-token: write
      contents: read
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Azure Login
        uses: azure/login@v1
        with:
          client-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_CLIENT_ID }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_TENANT_ID }}
          subscription-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID }}

      - name: Deploy Bicep
        uses: azure/arm-deploy@v1
        with:
          resourceGroupName: rg-${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }}
          template: main.bicep
          parameters: environment=${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }} projectName=myapp ownerTag=team-email

      - name: Deploy Function Code
        uses: Azure/functions-action@v1
        with:
          app-name: func-${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }}
          package: function-app/
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical understanding of observability in a lightweight Azure stack, covering frontend-backend instrumentation, tracing continuity, log routing, and alerting, plus a minimal CI/CD workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Application Insights integration in SPA and Azure Functions
- End-to-end tracing with correlation IDs
- Log Analytics workspace and log routing
- Alerts for latency spikes and error rates
- Cost considerations for observability including sampling strategies
- CI/CD wiring with GitHub Actions for Azure Static Web Apps and Functions

## Code Example

```javascript
// SPA: generate correlation ID and pass in requests
const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();

// Store in session for consistency
sessionStorage.setItem('correlationId', correlationId);

// Include in API requests
fetch('/api/data', {
  headers: {
    'x-correlation-id': correlationId
  }
});
```

```javascript
// Azure Function: read and log correlation ID
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || crypto.randomUUID();

  context.log.info('Processing request', { correlationId });

  context.res = {
    body: { data: [] },
    headers: { 'x-correlation-id': correlationId }
  };
};
```

## Cost Considerations

- **Application Insights**: Starts with 5 GB free per month; implement sampling (typically 10-30%) for high-traffic apps
- **Log Analytics**: Pay-per-GB ingestion; retention defaults to 30 days
- **Azure Static Web Apps**: Free tier available
- **Azure Functions**: Consumption plan with pay-per-execution pricing
- **Alerts**: First 10,000 alerts are free monthly

